2026-09-24 M1 self-review before the reviewer thread: (1) repo.mark_missing_out_of_universe refuses an empty key list and seed() refuses a snapshot below its M0-05 floor (config/universe_*.yaml min_count_check): `not (cik = any('{}'))` is true for every row, so a truncated download would have moved the whole universe out. (2) insider_events natural key includes value: one Form 4 can carry two same-day lots of equal size at different prices. (3) 0002 sets default privileges so tables added by later migrations are granted to service_role (Supabase parity) and stay closed to anon/authenticated. Each has a regression test.
2026-09-25 M2 SEC timestamps: submissions JSON acceptanceDateTime is UTC (3,057 of 3,082 F-US filings fit EDGAR's 17:30 ET next-day rule only as UTC); the SGML header ACCEPTANCE-DATETIME is US Eastern (Geron's 06:01:05 = the JSON's 11:01:05Z) and is converted. A missing timestamp falls back to the next day 00:00 UTC (never earlier than the real acceptance).
2026-09-25 M2 parsing with the standard library (json, xml.etree with DTDs refused, csv) instead of edgartools: the bulk companyfacts/submissions files, Form 4 XML and 13F TSVs are simple formats, and edgartools fetches over its own HTTP client, outside pipeline/net/http.py's allowlist and rate limits.
2026-09-25 M2 companyfacts: only 10-K/10-Q forms (and amendments) feed fundamentals; 8-K earnings exhibits are unaudited and often partial. The fiscal calendar comes from 10-K annual durations (most-reported start per end), dates only, so it cannot leak a value into the past.
2026-09-25 M2 concept fallback (§4.1.2 "→") is per period, not per company: a filer that moves from SalesRevenueNet to RevenueFromContract… keeps both eras. An alternative can be a summed list whose first concept is required (total_debt = long-term + commercial paper + short-term borrowings).
2026-09-25 M2 config/signals.yaml xbrl_map.total_debt (protected, needs human-approved): was [LongTermDebt, LongTermDebtNoncurrent, DebtCurrent], i.e. one concept, which gave Quanta $62.7M (real ≈ $4.2B) and Oracle $10.6B (real ≈ $92.6B). Now summed alternatives; tests/us/test_fus.py pins PWR 2024-12-31 = 4,162,436,000 and ORCL 2025-05-31 = 92,568,000,000.
2026-09-25 M2 restatement vs rounding: a later value that differs only by rounding (105,100,000,000 in a footnote vs 105,103,000,000 on the balance sheet; tables moved from thousands to millions) is not a restatement; the more precise value is kept. Needs >= 2 significant digits in the coarse value.
2026-09-25 M2 diluted shares are a weighted average, not additive: Q4 = 4 x FY - (Q1 + Q2 + Q3), and only when Q1-Q3 are each within 0.5-2x of FY; otherwise a split mixed bases (NVDA FY2024 gave 47.3B) and Q4 is left null with the reason logged.
2026-09-25 M2 fiscal labels: FY number anchored on the latest 10-K's own `fy` and counted along the calendar; per-filing `fy` tags are sometimes wrong (ORCL tagged Q1 FY2027 as 2026).
2026-09-25 M2 storage: fundamentals_q keeps the 60 most recent quarters per company (all versions); the Lab builds longer history from the raw files (§2.8).
2026-09-25 M2 Form 4: the reporting owners of one filing are one person for S7 (a fund and its GP filing jointly are one buyer); the derivative table is parsed but never stored; a filing that fails to parse is logged in the run's stats and the run is marked partial.
2026-09-25 M2 spin-offs: a Form 10-12B counts as effective at the first of an 8-K with item 5.01 or 3.03, an EFFECT notice for the 10-12B, or the registrant's first 10-Q/10-K. Registrants are remembered in a pending-registrations state file (Actions cache); if the cache is lost the daily run rebuilds it from the last 120 days of daily indexes. Parent = universe names mentioned >= 2 times in the Form 10 (two-word names or longer), top 3, unconfirmed.
2026-09-25 M2 13F: per filer the latest RESTATEMENT replaces the original and NEW HOLDINGS amendments add; 13F-NT holds nothing; put/call and PRN rows are dropped; a CUSIP whose rows mostly carry a non-common TITLEOFCLASS (preferred, warrants, rights, debt, options, units other than partnership common units) is dropped. Matching: exact normalized name, else rapidfuzz token_sort_ratio >= 92 with a unique best, else unmapped (logged in the run's stats, most-held first). filed_at = the day after the data set's filing window closes.
2026-09-25 M2 13F availability: data sets cover 3-month filing windows (Dec-Feb, Mar-May, Jun-Aug, Sep-Nov); the quarterly run takes the latest window closed >= 21 days ago. First production run: dispatch quarterly.yml with windows=3 so S8 has two quarters of growth.
2026-09-25 M2 runs: repo.tracked_run commits the runs row first, rolls back a failed job's writes and records the error; one bad company (weekly) or filing (daily) is logged and the run ends `partial`. The weekly sha256 state is written only after a company's rows commit, so a failed company is retried next week.
2026-09-25 M2 workflows daily.yml / weekly.yml / quarterly.yml (§2.5) with the US steps; each skips with a notice until the DATABASE_URL and SEC_USER_AGENT secrets exist, and applies pending migrations first. Order for the first production run: migrate -> seed -> weekly -> quarterly (windows=3).
2026-09-25 M2 repo.upsert_us_companies: a re-seed keeps SIC/sector/industry/fiscal year from the weekly run (coalesce) instead of blanking them; in_universe is re-decided by the next weekly run.
2026-09-25 M2 fixtures: companyfacts trimmed to the xbrl_map concepts and submissions to the forms M2 reads (scripts/fetch_fixtures.py f-us); expected CSVs and 13F expectations come from independent scripts (fixtures/us/expected/derive_expected.py, fixtures/us/13f/derive_expected.py) that don't import pipeline code. F-F4's synthetic cluster is generated by fixtures/us/form4/synthetic/generate.py.
2026-09-25 M2 local runs: PyPI is still blocked by the session's egress policy; pure tests ran locally (scratch venv + rapidfuzz's pure-Python fallback), ruff 0.15.8 and mypy 1.19.1 (from the uv cache) were run on the new modules, DB tests run in CI.
2026-09-25 M2 review round 1 (PR #4). F1: JsonSource indexes submissions.zip's older-filings pages once (the per-company sort of ~1M names would have taken ~70 min per weekly run); moved to pipeline/us/bulk.py.
2026-09-25 M2 review F2: SEC writes a day's master index at ~22:00 ET (02:00-03:00 UTC), after daily.yml's 01:30 UTC start, so the default run now catches up: it lists the quarter's published indexes (daily-index/YYYY/QTRn/index.json) and processes every day after the last one it finished (state file). A day not yet published is read by the next run instead of being skipped as a holiday; `--date` still runs one day.
2026-09-25 M2 review F3: a derived value (YTD difference, Q4 = FY - Q1..Q3, the diluted-shares Q4) is recomputed only when the larger period's value comes from a filing at least as recent as every value subtracted from it; otherwise the last consistent value is kept and the reason logged. On F-US: Apple FY2017 Q2 CFO has no value until the restated 12,570M (never the mixed 12,345M); CAT FY2015 Q4 operating income goes -114M -> -175M without the -289/-492/-704M swings. M2-02's example is now CAT's restated FY2015 Q4.
2026-09-25 M2 review F4: insider_events keep every filing as filed (a Form 4/A or a revised PIT disclosure is a second row; deleting the original would rewrite what was known before). Readers use pipeline/signals/insiders.latest_versions: per company, person and trade date, only the latest filing's trades count (S7 in M4).
2026-09-25 M2 review F5: the universe rule's TTM revenue is the sum of the known quarters of the last 12 months when fewer than 4 are known (a spin-off, an IPO, or a quarter left null by a sanity check). Revenue is never negative, so it is a lower bound: GE Vernova is in from its first 10-Q instead of ~10 months later, and nothing below $50M gets in on an estimate.
2026-09-25 M2 review F6: "common stock listed" (§1.3) is enforced two ways: a filer whose listed tickers are all preferred series (SCE-PB) is out, and so is one whose latest 10-K reports dei:EntityPublicFloat = 0 (a wholly-owned subsidiary with listed preferred shares or notes). Share classes such as BRK-B stay; no reported float (a new registrant) excludes nothing.
2026-09-25 M2 review F7: the guard's pit_rule now scans whole files (SQL split across lines), knows TABLE / COPY / USING and ORM .from_(), and flags a point-in-time table name used as a string value outside pit.py, repo.py (writes), size_guard.py (probes) and the guard itself. Seeded cases in tests/guard/cases (protected paths: this PR needs the human-approved label anyway).
2026-09-25 M2 review F8: every §4.1.5 null reason is written to .cache/us/issues.csv (uploaded by weekly.yml as the us-data-issues artifact); the run's stats keep counts per reason and 20 samples.
2026-09-25 M2 review F9: quarterly.yml runs 13F before the universe re-seed, so CUSIPs map against the universe the weekly run decided.
2026-09-25 M2 review F10: writing a company prunes its fundamentals_q versions the current code no longer produces and quarters outside the 60-quarter window (SQL function prune_fundamentals, migration 0004, so Python never names the table in a read). The M1-04 projection counts 1.4 versions per company-quarter (F-US measures 1.39 after F3).
2026-09-25 M2 review F9: a re-seed keeps the weekly run's universe decision (in_universe, excluded_reason); it re-admits only a company the snapshot step had moved out ("not in the SEC NYSE/Nasdaq snapshot") that is listed again. New companies enter as in_universe until the next weekly decides.
2026-09-25 M2 review F2: catch-up commits each day before moving the cursor. A day with failed downloads (network, or an index answering 403 on a weekday) holds the cursor so the next run re-reads it (inserts are idempotent); after 3 days it is passed with the errors in the run's stats (status partial).
2026-09-25 M2 review R2-F1: quarterize keeps two times per value: when a filing last changed it, and the latest filing that reported it (a repeat with an equal or rounding-equal value moves only the second). A derived value needs the minuend's latest report to be no earlier than each subtrahend's last change, so a 10-K repeating last year's FY after a restated quarter confirms the pair. F-US: 1.418 versions per quarter; size_guard projects 1.45. QUARTERIZE_VERSION 2 re-quarterizes every company on the next weekly run.
2026-09-25 M2 review R2-F2: fiscal-quarter ends are picked from fact counts (the end most facts report for a start and band, ties to the earlier date), never from set iteration order; the F-US output is identical under every hash seed.
2026-09-25 M2 review R2-F3: a 10-K public float of 0 excludes a filer only if it already filed a 10-K/10-Q by the float date (a subsidiary with listed notes or preferred). An IPO or spin-off listed after the float date reports 0 in its first 10-K and stays in. The weekly state stores the float date.
2026-09-25 M2 review R2-F4: the guard's table-name literal rule is case-insensitive; in repo.py a PIT table name may appear only as an _insert() target, in size_guard.py only where it names a probe table; size_guard's probe constants are flagged anywhere else. Protected path: needs the human-approved label.
2026-09-25 M2 review R2-F5: catch-up counts retries in runs (RETRY_RUNS = 3), not calendar days: Friday's index is first read on Tuesday. The daily state stores the held day and its attempts.
2026-09-25 M2 review R2-F6: a 403/404 on the current quarter's daily-index listing means nothing is published in it yet (SEC creates it hours into the quarter's first day); an earlier quarter's missing listing is logged and the run is partial.
2026-09-25 M2 review R2-F7: insider_events.amends (migration 0005) holds a Form 4/A's dateOfOriginalSubmission. latest_versions groups a US amendment with the original filed that day (Eastern) and keeps the latest amendment whole, so a corrected trade date counts once; separate original filings all count; India revisions (no link) still win per trade date.
2026-09-25 M3 NSE access from data-centre IPs is intermittent: the home page answers 403 while the APIs often answer without its cookies; bursts of ~20 requests get "Access Denied" for minutes. NseClient: warm-up failures are ignored; a block is any 401/403/429 response; one retry on a rebuilt session, then backoff; 3 consecutive blocks -> stale for the run (source_health 'nse' stale). NSE also answers 403 for a missing archive file, so the bhavcopy chain asks BSE first whether a day traded (BSE answers a missing file with its home page, status 200).
2026-09-25 M3 India prices are written by M3 (§4.4 "India: all EQ closes from the bhavcopy -> prices_w"): week_end = the Friday, close = the last trading day's close, adj_close = close until M4's split detection; BSE rows are matched by ISIN (BSE files carry groups, not NSE series), NSE/manual rows by symbol. prices_w.source = nse_bhavcopy | bse_bhavcopy | manual_bhavcopy.
2026-09-25 M3 results: SEBI Integrated Filing - Financials (API integrated-filing-results, taxonomy in-capmkt) since FY2025 Q4, the legacy results API/taxonomy (in-bse-fin) before; both read by local element name through ind_as_map. The quarter is the 3-month context ending at the report date (found by dates, not context ids); consolidated beats standalone for the same quarter; a revision is a new row version; filed_at = the listing's creation_Date (IST) in UTC.
2026-09-25 M3 India half-yearly items in fundamentals_q: balance-sheet columns only on Q2/Q4 rows; cfo/capex are half-year flows (Q2 row = H1, Q4 row = H2 = FY - H1 on the same basis, else null; Q1/Q3 null), so TTM CFO = H1 + H2. shares_outstanding = paid-up equity capital / face value (both in every results filing). op_income = PBT + finance costs - other income (ind_as_map), null unless all three are known.
2026-09-25 M3 shareholding -> ownership_q in percent (config thresholds are percent): promoter_pledged_pct = pledged shares / promoter holding (R5's measure); fii_pct = FPI category I + II (a foreign strategic holder such as JSW's JFE is not portfolio money; foreign-institutions total as fallback); dii_pct = domestic institutions; inst_pct = domestic + foreign institutions; filed_at = the listing's broadcast time; source 'nse_shp'.
2026-09-25 M3 insider trading: NSE replaced the corporates-pit API (now always empty) with corporates-pit-gg, an index of disclosures; each trade is in the disclosure's XBRL. Kept: promoter/promoter-group equity market purchases and sales (+ pledge creation/revocation if disclosed). Gifts, off-market/inter-se transfers, conversions, ESOPs, invocations and non-promoter trades are dropped. A disclosure repeated line for line is one event (natural key). India has no trading-plan flag, so planned=false.
2026-09-25 M3 pledge events come from consecutive quarterly shareholding patterns (change in pledged shares -> pledge_created / pledge_released at the quarter end), not event-by-event SAST Reg 31 filings: no §4.6-4.7 rule needs finer dates, and it needs no extra source.
2026-09-25 M3 universe (weekly): the NSE securities list (floor-checked like the seed) upserts companies and moves missing ones out; ASM/GSM listings take companies out with the reason "surveillance: <list> stage <n>"; if the lists can't be fetched, last week's flags stay. Re-seeding keeps sector/industry (coalesce), as for the US.
2026-09-25 M3 request budget: XBRL downloads are capped at 400 per weekly run (results + shareholding, new filings first) and 80 per daily run (insider trading); the rest waits in a state file (Actions cache). History: the weekly run also queues the integrated-filing history (~6 quarters) of 60 companies per run, capex desk first, then by traded value.
2026-09-25 M3 manual imports accept the two bhavcopy CSV formats (UDiFF, and NSE's full security-wise bhavcopy); the insider-trading CSV is only an index of XBRL links, so it can't stand in for the network.
2026-09-25 M3 F-IN was fetched from this session with scripts/fetch_fixtures.py f-in (resumable, cool-down on blocks); one round of blocks cleared after ~4 minutes.
2026-09-25 M3: the M2 re-seed rule (review F9) covers India too: upsert_in_companies keeps the weekly ASM/GSM decision, so a failed surveillance fetch keeps last week's flags and the quarterly seed lets no one back in.
2026-09-25 M4 S7: "unplanned code-P buys of >= $25k each" = each insider's buys in the 60-day window total >= $25k; the $250k total sums those insiders. Amended Form 4s count once (insiders.latest_versions).
2026-09-25 M4 S8: strength clip(growth / 0.5) uses the latest quarter's holder growth; revenue-size deciles rank the US universe by TTM revenue as of the week, and the holder percentile is taken within the company's decile (ties half).
2026-09-25 M4 S9: qualifying facts are counted once per (fact_type, subject_key), so a statement repeated in a press release and a 10-Q counts once. governance_flag subject keys end in ":added" / ":removed" (removal -> S9, added going_concern / material_weakness -> R3); the facts pipeline (M5) follows this.
2026-09-25 M4 S12: "each of the last 3 fiscal years" uses trailing 4-quarter windows at lags 0, 4 and 8 of each company, so a sector mixing fiscal year-ends lines up; sector medians are across the market's companies in that sector as of the week. India has no industry data yet, so India S12 reports its sector as missing.
2026-09-25 M4 windows: look-back windows include their first day ("<= 18 months ago" includes exactly 18 months).
2026-09-25 M4 shared definitions: invested capital treats a missing debt figure as no debt (filers without borrowings report no debt concept); net debt (S5, S6, R6) needs a reported debt figure. India half-yearly flows/points follow M3's layout (TTM CFO = H1 + H2; balance-sheet points are the latest value within 2 quarters).
2026-09-25 M4 R2: receivables growth (quarter end vs a year earlier) is compared with TTM revenue growth. R4: acquisition evidence is a US 8-K item 2.01 (new corp_events kind 'acquisition', migration 0007) or an Indian announcement mentioning an acquisition or amalgamation, in the last 12 months. R5 RPT reads a fact with subject key related_party:revenue_pct. R6 for India uses 2 half-year steps (the same 4 quarters).
2026-09-25 M4 scores: a family "fired" when its weighted contribution is > 0 (a signal weighted 0 by the Lab doesn't count toward the 2-family rule). Early = 40 <= Evidence < 60. The candidate-stage market-cap floor (§1.3) sends companies below it, or without a price, to 'none' rather than candidate / priced_in / early.
2026-09-25 M4 novelty: "not seen in the last 12 weeks" = not in the shortlist of any of the previous 12 weeks (new table shortlists). A candidate ranked 11th is not "seen" and stays eligible.
2026-09-25 M4 C1: needs >= 52 weekly points; each week's EV uses the fundamentals known that week (pit.AsOf.fundamental_versions + select_as_of). Percentile rank = share below + half the ties. C2: "latest revenue YoY" is the latest quarter's YoY (TTM YoY if that quarter lacks a year-ago match); the 5-year OPM median is over the 20 quarterly TTM values; S2C uses annual steps.
2026-09-25 M4 C4: GDELT asks for one request every 5 s, so a run makes at most 100 new queries (~8 min) and reuses a count under 28 days old; the query is the quoted short name plus (ticker OR Inc/Ltd), tickers under 3 characters dropped (GDELT rejects them).
2026-09-25 M4 prices: US candidates get their whole Stooq history (up to 10 years, for C1) in prices_w; manual fallback imports/us_prices/<TICKER>.csv in Stooq's format. India benchmarks (NIFTY 50/500) come from NSE's ind_close_all file for the bhavcopy's trading day, fetched by the India weekly job; their 52-week history builds up week by week.
2026-09-25 M4 splits: a price jump within 3% of a split ratio is adjusted only when consecutive share counts show the same ratio (window: 30 days before the last old-count period end to 120 days after the first new-count one); an unmatched jump is flagged in the run stats and left alone. A share split with no price jump means the source was already adjusted (Stooq), and older share counts are scaled to today's basis for market caps.
2026-09-25 M4 storage (SPEC_ISSUES 9, as proposed): signal_values keeps every row for the latest week only; older weeks keep fired rows plus the first unfired row after a streak. Unknown red flags are kept for the latest week only, 'none' scores for 13 weeks, everything for 3 years.
2026-09-25 M4 screener API: screener_v (latest scored week, one row per company) and screen(spec jsonb), a fixed set of optional filters (market, desk, sector, buckets, min Evidence/Gap, signals, families, hard flags, metric thresholds); pipeline/screener.py ScreenSpec is the contract the web app mirrors. company_metrics holds the latest per-company metrics.
2026-09-25 M4 pipeline: weekly.yml gains a `scores` job after the US and India jobs (it runs if either succeeded). S10 for India needs demerger/rights-issue events, which arrive with announcement triage (P-07, M5); S11 stays quiet until the Capex Desk (M5) confirms memberships.
2026-09-25 M3 review F1: the weekly state keeps each company's parsed results of its last 3 financial years, whole years (a Q4 row's H2 = FY - H1 needs that year's H1); a run writes only the rows of the financial years its new filings touched, through a fill-only upsert (a null never replaces a stored value). A later year arriving no longer rebuilds an old Q4 without its H1.
