2026-09-25 M5 review R2-F1/F2: V1-TYPE reads the sentence around the grounded quote in the canonical text, clause by clause: a number fails when its clause names a share-price topic (stock/share price, TSR, common stock up/down, buybacks, dividends declared or paid, EPS, analyst ratings), or when its clause only modifies the previous one ("..., up 14% from a year ago") and that one does. Plain words elsewhere in the sentence ("upgraded our plant", "analysts had modeled", "continuing to pay dividends") don't reject a business fact.
